; A per-unit cost stated against no units.
;
; `{50.00 CAD}` is the single brace — the cost of one unit. A posting held at
; cost is worth `units × cost`, which is 0 here, so nothing is being lost and
; there is nothing to refuse. This is the counter-case to
; beancount_cost_total_against_no_units.beancount, where the doubled brace
; states the total and has nowhere to attach it.
;
; What this fixture produces: one transaction, two splits, both worth nothing,
; and no Imbalance.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
